all right  fetty jose on twitter wants to know  does ryan fitzpatrick win with the  cowboys roster should the cowboys trade  for him shireen  your thoughts  yeah they'd be much better off i think  but i'm ready for the cowboys to tank  for tua i mean i mean tank for two  tank for trevor two of us last year to  tank for trevor that's what i want to  see i want to see them in that position  to have to make a decision do we go with  dak prescott or we do we go for trevor  lawrence but i don't think they're gonna  get the first pick i do think they have  a top five pick they've moved up there  now after the loss uh last night but  yeah i think ryan fitzpatrick would win  some games for him but at this point  mike what are you playing for in in 2020  i mean they're not going to win a super  bowl right so get the draft pick  yeah look hey i'm a firm believer in  that that you know and it's the great  disconnect in the nfl we we talk all the  time about how everyone wants to win  every single game possible and then when  we see the final draft order we realize  how valuable it is to be higher on the  list and what teams will give up just to  move a few spots so yes once you know  it's over once you know it's done  there's no benefit in winning evaluate  your young players put your backups out  there see what the future holds by way  of the guys who otherwise aren't good  enough to play and then nature will take  its course and you will lose enough  games and maybe you're in position to  get trevor lawrence and dallas which  would create  quite  quite quite a situation in dallas if  they're in position to get trevor  lawrence and they have to decide what to  do with dak prescott but look i agree  with you fitzpatrick is better than ben  denucci he's better than andy dalton  frankly and i put the poll question up  last monday when it was obvious andy  dalton wouldn't be able to play last  week who helps the cowboys win sunday  night ben dinucci garrett gilbert or  colin kaepernick and 47 000 votes came  in and 60 said kaepernick now it wasn't  going to happen  because of the covet protocols you're  not going to be cleared  to to play by sunday and even if you are  you're not going to practice by then but  uh  look  you get what you deserve when you trot  out ben dinucci and garrett gilbert as  your top two quarterbacks and maybe  they're already implementing the tanking  strategy maybe the joke's on everyone  else because maybe the cowboys are  winning by losing all right one more  quick one a red zone out is it time to  accept that carson wentz  is what he is talented but inconsistent  something's happened to him mike i just  i don't know what it is but 14  interceptions is the most he's ever  thrown in a season that was his rookie  he has 12 this season along with 12  touchdowns he's lost four fumbles he's  not the same guy and to say ben and ucci  outplayed him last night i wouldn't go  that far  but it wasn't far off i mean there  wasn't a big gap there he's just not  playing very well for whatever reason  and they have a big rehab project or  they're gonna have to move on from him  he strikes me as a guy who is trying too  hard to validate the decisions that have  been made by the eagles in him trading  up in 2016 to get him in the second spot  of the draft picking him over nick foles  after folz became a super bowl mvp and  almost got the eagles back to the nfc  championship game the following year and  that's when the eagles said sea and nick  were sticking with carson wentz and then  they give carson wentz the huge contract  i feel like he believes he can reverse  everyone's perception of him with one  throw and he's constantly trying to make  that one throw and he's trying too hard  and he's going it's it's almost like the  jameis winston trying to do more than  you're physically capable of doing and  it leads to outcomes that make people  say  why is that guy  on the football field and if he keeps it  up he's not going to be 